(4) THE R-TRANSFORM IS THE DIVERGENT FACTORIAL SERIES (ADD-6 resurgence source):
    R(z) = sum_{n>=1} kappa_n z^{n-1} = sum_{n>=1} n! z^{n-1} = 1 + 2z + 6z^2 + 24z^3 + ...
    Gevrey-1 / Borel sum = exp-integral; this IS the wildness ADD-6 saw in U(x,y).
      [z^0] R = 1
      [z^1] R = 2
      [z^2] R = 6
      [z^3] R = 24
      [z^4] R = 120
      [z^5] R = 720
      [z^6] R = 5040

(5) SHARPEN ADD-4: the over-count IS the CLASSICAL moments A000262 (sets of lists).
    SAME cumulants kappa_n=n!:  classical moments = Sum_{ALL partitions} prod|B|!
    = A000262 (EGF exp(x/(1-x)), 'sets of lists');  free moments = Sum_{NC} = A088368
    ('sets of NONcrossing lists').  The crossing partitions = the classical<->free gap.
   k=1:  free NC-sum=       1=A088368   classical ALL-sum=        1=A000262   crossing(class-free)=        0
   k=2:  free NC-sum=       3=A088368   classical ALL-sum=        3=A000262   crossing(class-free)=        0
   k=3:  free NC-sum=      13=A088368   classical ALL-sum=       13=A000262   crossing(class-free)=        0
   k=4:  free NC-sum=      69=A088368   classical ALL-sum=       73=A000262   crossing(class-free)=        4
   k=5:  free NC-sum=     421=A088368   classical ALL-sum=      501=A000262   crossing(class-free)=       80
   k=6:  free NC-sum=    2867=A088368   classical ALL-sum=     4051=A000262   crossing(class-free)=     1184
   k=7:  free NC-sum=   21477=A088368   classical ALL-sum=    37633=A000262   crossing(class-free)=    16156

(6) THE e-ASYMPTOTIC IS A FREE-PROBABILITY STATEMENT ABOUT THE FACTORIAL LAW:
    m_k / k! = A088368(k)/k! -> e  (Kotesovec). The factorial law's free moments
    grow like e*k!: a clean meaning for the 'wild end' constant e.
